    "Prioritize back volume next week by adding at least 2 extra sets of rowing movements, aiming to bring back sets up to 6 or more, which should help reverse the 5-point strength index drop and restore structural balance with all your pressing work.",
    "Keep riding the chest momentum by maintaining your current bench press loading and rep scheme — a 6-point index jump in one week is excellent and you want to build on that consistency rather than change anything.",
    "Add one extra set of biceps work, such as a curl variation, to bring that group closer to 3 to 4 sets per week and support long-term elbow and shoulder joint health as bench press loads continue to increase.",
    "Monitor how your back feels during and after rowing sets next week — if it feels consistently fatigued or performance drops again, consider whether your chest and back sessions need to be separated by an extra rest day."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Big chest and triceps strength gains this week drove bench press progress, but back strength dropped 5 points and needs extra volume and attention next period to restore balance."
}
